 2          0.000e+00            0.366025               True
 3          0.000e+00            0.504623               True
 4          0.000e+00            0.581861               True

[4] reading
    * tree mass is strictly LARGER than the lattice mass at every matched beta;
    * at beta_c^lat the lattice is gapless (m=0) but the tree is massive
      => the implication 'm_tree>0 => m_lat>0' is FALSE in an exactly solvable model.
    * direction of the surviving strict inequality:  m_tree >= m_lat  (UPPER bound
      on the lattice mass out of a tree mass)  -> useless for a gap lower bound.
    * NOTE the contrast with the ferromagnetic Ising case (bc_ising.py), where the
      sign is OPPOSITE: the sign is not a geometric fact, it is FKG-dependent.
